---
import BaseLayout from "@ui/components/core/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import type { Metadata } from "@ui/components/core/seo/types";
import "@ui/components/legal/legal.css";

const TITLE = "Privacy Policy: ContribKit";
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "2026-09-16";

const metadata: Metadata = { title: TITLE, robots: "noindex, nofollow" };
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="legal-header">
        <a href="/" data-astro-prefetch="false" class="back-link mono link-action">← back</a>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="dimmer mono">Effective date: {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-body">

        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>ContribKit is a tool for visualising public GitHub contribution calendars. This policy explains what data we collect, why, and how you can control it, both in the mobile app and on this website.</p>

        <h2>The mobile app</h2>
        <p>The ContribKit app (iOS &amp; Android) requires no account, login, or authentication token. Your username, selected year, palette, and visual preferences are stored locally on your device and are never sent to us. Uninstalling the app, or clearing its data, removes them.</p>
        <p>There is exactly one thing the app sends to a server of ours, and only when you ask it to: a message you write in the app's <strong>Contact</strong> sheet. It is covered by the <a href="#contact-form">Contact form</a> section below, which applies to the app and the website alike. Apart from that, we operate no server that receives or stores your personal data.</p>
        <p>To function, the app connects to two third parties directly from your device:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong>: the app requests the public contribution page at <code>github.com/users/&#123;username&#125;/contributions</code> using only the username you enter. As with any web request, GitHub receives your device's IP address and standard request metadata. No GitHub login or token is involved.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong>: on first launch the app downloads its typefaces (Inter, JetBrains Mono) from Google's servers, which receive your IP address; the fonts are then cached on your device. This is subject to <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The app contains no advertising. We do not track you across other apps or websites, and we do not use advertising identifiers (such as Apple's IDFA or the Android Advertising ID).</p>

        <h3>Crash reports and usage events (in the app)</h3>
        <p>The app can report defects and record which of its screens are used and which options are chosen in them. Both are optional, both are controlled from the <strong>Privacy</strong> sheet in the app, and both are processed in the European Union.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Crash reports</strong>, via <a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sentry</a>. Sent unless you turn them off. A report contains the <em>type</em> of the error and the point in our code where it happened, plus your device model and OS version. When the error happens while the app is open, the report also includes a short, low-resolution recording of the app's screens in the moments before it, in which every piece of text, every image and the whole contribution calendar are drawn as plain rectangles; nothing is recorded when no error occurs. A report never contains the error's message, the username you looked up, or any calendar data: the message is replaced, and the recording is masked, before either leaves your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage events</strong>, via <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PostHog</a>. Off until you turn them on. An event is a name from a fixed list, such as "the Customizer was opened", together with the option it concerns when there is one, such as the palette, cell shape, export format or year that was chosen, each drawn from a fixed set. It never carries the username you looked up, any free text, or any calendar data. PostHog does attach a randomly generated identifier to each event so that repeated events from one installation are not counted as many; it is created on your device, is not linked to you or to any account, and is discarded if you turn usage events off. No user profile is created, and PostHog records no session and receives no recording.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Neither is linked to an identity, neither is used for advertising, and neither is shared with anyone. You can change either choice at any time; turning one off stops it immediately.</p>

        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>The ContribKit website (<code>contribkit.app</code>) uses the following services to understand traffic and improve the site. The analytics services below are loaded only after you give explicit consent via the cookie banner.</p>

        <h3>Site preferences (strictly necessary)</h3>
        <p>To remember the last GitHub username you viewed between visits, we store it in a first-party cookie (<code>ck_user</code>, expiry: 1 week) in your own browser. It holds only the username you entered, is never sent to any third party, and is not used for tracking or advertising. Because it is essential to providing this feature, it does not require consent; you can remove it at any time by clearing your browser's cookies.</p>

        <h3>Google Analytics (GA4)</h3>
        <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to measure page views, session duration, navigation paths, and usage events: a name from a fixed list, such as "a palette was chosen", together with the option it concerns (the palette, cell shape, export format or year), never the username you looked up. Each event is listed in the <a href="https://github.com/fbuireu/contribkit/wiki/Web-Application" target="_blank" rel="noopener">project wiki</a>. IP addresses are anonymised before storage. Data is processed by Google LLC and subject to <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>. Cookies set: <code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code> (expiry: 2 years).</p>

        <h3>Better Stack Telemetry</h3>
        <p>We use Better Stack to monitor site performance, catch front-end errors, and receive the same usage events as Google Analytics. Session data is anonymous and not linked to any individual. Data is processed by Better Stack, Inc. and subject to <a href="https://betterstack.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Better Stack's Privacy Policy</a>. Cookies set: <code>bs_*</code> (session cookies).</p>

        <h2 id="contact-form">Contact form</h2>
        <p>The <a href="/contact">contact form</a> on this website, and the <strong>Contact</strong> sheet in the app, are the one place ContribKit asks you to type something that is sent to us rather than to GitHub. Both collect your <strong>email address</strong>, your <strong>message</strong>, and your <strong>name</strong> if you choose to give one. Nothing else is attached: no account, no identifier, and none of the calendar you were looking at. The app's sheet sends the same three fields to the same endpoint on this website.</p>
        <p>A submission reaches our Cloudflare Worker, which turns it into an email and hands it to Cloudflare Email Routing, which forwards it to the maintainer's mailbox. <strong>Nothing is stored on the server</strong>: the message is not written to a database or a log, and the only copy that survives is the email itself. That copy is kept in the mailbox for as long as it takes to answer you and is deleted on request. It is used to reply to you and for nothing else: never for a mailing list, never for advertising, and it is never shared.</p>
        <p>A hidden field and a per-IP limit of five submissions a minute are used to refuse automated submissions. Cloudflare acts as our processor for the delivery; see <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>You can accept or reject analytics cookies at any time using the cookie banner or the <button type="button" data-cc="show-preferencesModal" class="inline-prefs-btn">cookie preferences</button> link in the footer. Rejecting analytics means neither Google Analytics nor Better Stack will load.</p>

        <h2>In-app purchases</h2>
        <p>Tips are optional. Payments are processed entirely by Apple (App Store) or Google (Play Store); we never receive or store your payment details.</p>
        <p>To deliver and restore purchases, the app uses RevenueCat (RevenueCat, Inc.) as its purchase-infrastructure provider. RevenueCat assigns an anonymous, randomly generated app user ID and receives device and transaction information (device model, OS version, IP address, and purchase history) solely to provide this functionality. It is not used for advertising or cross-app tracking. See <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RevenueCat's Privacy Policy</a>. You can request deletion of your RevenueCat data by contacting us.</p>

        <h2>Data retention</h2>
        <p>App preferences remain on your device until you clear the app's data or uninstall it. Google Analytics data is retained for 14 months, after which it is automatically deleted. Better Stack telemetry is retained for 30 days. Sentry crash reports and PostHog usage events are retained according to each provider's project settings and are deleted on request. RevenueCat retains purchase records for as long as needed to provide and restore purchases. We retain no other personal data.</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, you have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, or object to the processing of your personal data, and to data portability. Because the app keeps your preferences only on your device, you can exercise most of these directly by clearing the app's data or uninstalling it. For website analytics, crash reports, usage events or RevenueCat data, email <a href="mailto:contact@contribkit.app">contact@contribkit.app</a>.</p>
        <p>The data controller is the owner identified in the <a href="/legal-notice">Legal Notice</a>. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your supervisory authority. In Spain, the Agencia Española de Protección de Datos (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AEPD</a>).</p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>ContribKit is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy to reflect changes in the services we use. The effective date above reflects the most recent revision. Continued use after an update constitutes acceptance.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy? Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, or mail <a href="mailto:contact@contribkit.app">contact@contribkit.app</a>.</p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
